<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="GiantSteps-B-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1959
Composer:	John Coltrane
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	16-bar form
Style:	Fast swing; hard bop
Key:	B major (with rapid shifts among B, G,
                          and Eb major)

Coltrane composed “Giant Steps” during his 1959 Atlantic
recording sessions; it was first recorded that year and
released on the album Giant Steps in 1960. Its rapid
movement through three distant key centers became
known as “Coltrane changes,” making the tune a
landmark—and a famously demanding improvisation
vehicle—in modern jazz. </spComments>
